  "details": "less of a feature request, more of a feature improvement suggestion, but i'm sure this is suitable for here.\n\ni find the out-of-body experience holoport locomotion creates by rendering your avatar as a moving statue very disorienting.\n\nthis also isn't ideal in that others see you in that fixed pose, and while this does look pretty goofy and lots of fun has been had with it, it's also pretty awkward and janky for an accessibility feature.\n\ni suggest the following:\n\n(1): a setting to turn off the third person avatar in holoport, making your avatar invisible to yourself while locomoting\n\n(2): a feature that your avatar continues updating its pose as normal while locomoting.\n\n(1) should definitely be optional, i'm sure most holoport users are very used to using the third person avatar to understand where they're going, and with (2) implemented it would be especially useful for being aware of how others see you.\n\n(2) would probably be fine to have on by default, but maybe it would be best for it also be optional for the sake of privacy (and goofing around)",
